---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import StaticHeader from '../components/StaticHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import { getTreeData } from '../lib/content';

const { settings, branches, nodes } = await getTreeData();
---

<Base title="About · Dovahkiin">
  <StaticHeader />
  <main class="page prose">
    <h1>About</h1>
    <hr class="sk-rule" />
    <p class="disclaimer-box"><strong>{settings.disclaimer}</strong> {settings.footer}</p>

    <h2>What is this?</h2>
    <p>
      Dovahkiin turns your baby's first two years into an RPG-style skill tree. Birth is at the top and age increases as you
      scroll down. Each column is a branch of development, and each star is a skill. Prerequisites are drawn as constellation lines.
    </p>
    <p>
      Enter your baby's date of birth and the tree shows what they've unlocked, what they might be ready for now, and what's coming
      up. Every skill comes with <em>dad quests</em>: things to prepare, play and make safe before the next big moment arrives.
    </p>

    <h2>How to read the stars</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Small star</strong>: a skill. <strong>Large star</strong>: a milestone. <strong>Diamond</strong>: a keystone, like first steps.</li>
      <li><strong>Dim with a lock</strong>: locked for now. <strong>Dashed ring with a clock</strong>: coming up soon.</li>
      <li><strong>Dashed ring with an hourglass</strong>: old enough, but it usually comes after another skill.</li>
      <li><strong>Pulsing ring with sparkles</strong>: ready now. <strong>Bright and glowing with a tick</strong>: unlocked.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Age windows are broad on purpose. Plenty of babies reach skills at the far ends of a window, and some skip steps entirely (lots of
      babies never crawl). There's no "late" here.
    </p>

    <h2>Born early?</h2>
    <p>
      If you add a due date that's more than two weeks after the date of birth, the tree uses <strong>corrected age</strong> (age from
      the due date) until your baby's actual age reaches two years.
    </p>

    <h2>Where the ages come from</h2>
    <p>
      Age windows are based on public-health sources: the CDC's "Learn the Signs. Act Early." milestone checklists, the WHO Multicentre
      Growth Reference Study's windows of achievement for gross-motor milestones, and NHS guidance (including weaning and baby-proofing).
      Safe-sleep quests follow the Lullaby Trust. Each skill lists its sources.
    </p>

    <h2>Privacy</h2>
    <p>
      Your baby's details and progress are stored only in this browser (localStorage). Nothing is sent to a server, and there are no
      trackers. You can export, import or reset your progress from the settings menu.
    </p>

    <h2>The tree</h2>
    <p>{nodes.length} skills across {branches.length} branches: {branches.map((b) => b.name).join(', ')}.</p>
  </main>
  <SiteFooter />
</Base>

<style>
  .disclaimer-box {
    padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--panel-border);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--gold);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--panel);
    color: var(--ink);
  }
</style>
